{
  "reviews": {
    "node-n9epbz": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims sampling intervals introduce uncertainty about whether an upstream valve closed or a leak occurred between samples. The evidence (IA-P01) explicitly states the export supplies sampled values and does not include data from all locations or valve states. However, it also notes that P-U remained stable while P-R dropped significantly at 10:00:11. This pattern supports an interruption downstream of P-U but upstream of P-R (e.g., a closed valve between the two points). The node's claim is partially supported by evidence showing discrete drops and lack of continuous waveform, but it overstates uncertainty about 'upstream vs leak' without ruling out known distribution topology constraints.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A schematic or point register mapping P-U to P-R with intermediate valve states (if any) between the two measurement points. Evidence that would confirm whether a closed valve is plausible given normal operation and maintenance boundaries.","question":"Does the system design include an isolation valve between P-U and P-R, and if so, was it known or expected to be open during this event?"
    },
    "node-6t2yyp": {
      "supported": true,
      "issue": "",
      "evidenceNeeded": "",
      "question": ""
    },
    "node-mz6bl6": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims the shift log records 'boundary preparation in progress' but does not identify point of interruption or valve states. The evidence (IA-S01) confirms that at 09:48 crew U-A/U-B were at gallery with boundary preparation pending release; however it also notes RHOB observed an air-low indication and requested Utilities attendance, then work was paused at 10:02 without line opening authorized. This implies the interruption occurred before authorization or during unapproved activity. The node's claim is partially supported but incomplete because it does not address whether 'boundary preparation' included any valve operations that could have caused the drop.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Documentation of what activities constitute 'boundary preparation in progress' and which valves, if any, are operated under this status.","question":"What specific actions or valve manipulations were part of 'boundary preparation in progress' at 09:48?"
    }
  },
  "decision": {
    "summary": "Three nodes require attention. Node-n9epbz is partially supported but overstates uncertainty; node-6t2yyp stands as fully supported with no issue; node-mz6bl6 needs clarification on what 'boundary preparation' entails to assess whether valve states were relevant.",
    "evidenceUsed": ["IA-P01_pressure_and_alarm_extract.md", "IA-S01_shift_and_notification_log.md", "IA-D01_area_and_service_directory.md"],
    "unknowns": [
      "Whether an isolation valve exists between P-U and P-R",
      "What activities constitute 'boundary preparation in progress'",
      "If any valves were operated during boundary preparation"
    ],
    "alternatives": [
      "The pressure drop was caused by a leak downstream of P-U but upstream of P-R.",
      "A valve between P-U and P-R closed due to maintenance or error."
    ],"confidence": 0.75}
  }
